<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Livonian War</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Livonian War was a conflict from 1558 to 1583 over control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, fought by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> against Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. The war encouraged the closer union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Lithuania, which led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> in 1569 and the formation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. It ended with Russia failing to keep its Baltic conquests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/livonian-war.jpg" alt="Livonian War" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boris Chorikov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_Narva_1558.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
